From 7f430ed22e4208efb3e8fd06c36726c19b4187bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vignesh Viswanathan <viswanat@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Tue, 21 Apr 2026 00:47:18 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] mhi: Optimize firmware memory with RO segment sharing
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

When multiple MHI endpoints use the same firmware image, significant
memory can be saved by sharing read-only (RO) segments across endpoints
while allocating separate read-write (RW) segments for each.

This patch implements ELF-based firmware loading that:
- Analyzes ELF program headers to identify RO/RW boundary
- Shares RO segments globally across all endpoints
- Allocates RW segments per-endpoint
- Uses refcounting for proper cleanup

The optimization is controlled via the elf_fw_optimization flag in
mhi_controller, allowing client drivers to opt-in. When enabled:
- First endpoint: Allocates all segments, saves RO for sharing
- Subsequent endpoints: Reuse shared RO, allocate only RW segments

Memory savings scale with number of endpoints. For example, with
3 endpoints using 24MB firmware (16MB RO + 8MB RW):
- Without optimization: 72MB (24MB × 3)
- With optimization: 40MB (16MB shared + 8MB × 3)
- Savings: 44% reduction

The implementation handles two ELF scenarios:
1. Dual-ELF: SBL + WLAN firmware in single file
2. Single large ELF with RO/RW segments

Change-Id: I891268d147f1abf1d364d14146ccd933a359f9b2
Signed-off-by: Vignesh Viswanathan <viswanat@qti.qualcomm.com>
